            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal), according to Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal), according to Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal), petitioners argue that background checks are a standard practice, required for civil\u2011service employees since 1953 and for contractors since 2005."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal), according to Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal), according to Petitioners (General Neal K. Katyal), petitioners contend that the government may collect information as long as it is not disseminated in the employment context."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Respondents, respondents state that NASA does not use the employee\u2011suitability chart for contractor credentialing decisions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondents argue that open\u2011ended questions are necessary to identify \u201cpressure points\u201d in an applicant\u2019s background."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondents maintain that a narrow rule\u2014background checks with safeguards\u2014does not violate any constitutional right to informational privacy, citing the Ninth Circuit\u2019s Whalen decision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked what test should limit the kinds of questions the government may ask in the employment context, suggesting a scenario that includes diet, smoking, reading habits, hobbies, entertainment, and sexual practices."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "969b9f7f92feb3e68b234be0d899605cbae19588f26eac707e64daa047115472",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-969b9f7f92fe-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked whether every employee who is rejected will know the reason for the rejection."
      }
    ],
